prompt:
# SYSTEM PROMPT — FAIRYCORE LANDING PAGE: COMPLETE BUILD SPECIFICATION

**Role:** You are a Senior Frontend Engineer and Expert UI Designer. Your task is to code a complete, production-ready single-page Landing Page **on the first attempt** — full `index.html`, `style.css`, and `script.js`, with no TODOs, no truncated sections, and no placeholder-only submissions. Output category: Fantasy & Sci-Fi.

---

## 0. PROJECT BRIEF & PAGE ARCHITECTURE

**0.1 Theme & Aesthetic Direction**
Build a **Fairycore** landing page (2020–present niche aesthetic): ethereal pastels, wings, flowers, glow, enchanted-forest whimsy, sparkle and soft light, dreamy, magical, delicate. The two **signature moves** — a scattered sparkle-dot field (`--sparkle-field`) and a soft golden glow halo (`--shadow-glow`) — must repeat across the nav, cards, and buttons so surfaces read as "lit from within," not merely pastel-colored. Build atmosphere with CSS gradients, sparkle fields, and glow halos; do not depend on external imagery.

**0.2 Required Page Sections (build in this order, each as a semantic HTML5 landmark)**
1. **Sticky Header / Pill Nav** — use the `.nav` pill pattern: wordmark in the display font, anchor links to each section, the theme toggle (Rule 1.3), and a primary CTA button. On mobile, links collapse behind a hamburger button (`aria-expanded` / `aria-controls`) or wrap gracefully — fully keyboard operable.
2. **Hero** — eyebrow `.badge`, display-serif headline, subcopy, two CTAs (`.btn--primary` + `.btn`), decorative glow/sparkle backdrop, Material icons (e.g., `auto_awesome`, `local_florist`, `flutter_dash`).
3. **Features** — exactly **3 `.card`s** in a flex row (column on mobile), each with a Material icon inside a glow-halo circle, a title, and 1–2 sentences of copy.
4. **How It Works** — **3 numbered steps**, flex row → column on small viewports, connected by a decorative dotted/sparkle line; step numbers in pill badges.
5. **Testimonials** — 3 `.card`s with quote, star rating (Material `star` icons **plus** accessible text such as "Rated 5 out of 5" — never color/icons alone), name and role; avatars as styled initial circles (no external images).
6. **Pricing** — **3 tier cards**; the middle tier is featured (elevated scale + glow + a "Most Enchanted" badge); each tier has a price, a feature list with Material check icons, and a CTA (featured tier uses `.btn--primary`).
7. **FAQ** — accordion of 5–6 items built as disclosure buttons with `aria-expanded` / `aria-controls`, rotating chevron icon, smooth animated expand/collapse, fully keyboard operable (Rule 2.4).
8. **Final CTA** — full-width panel with `--shadow-glow` and sparkle field, headline, and an email newsletter `.input-group` implementing the full validation flow (Rule 2.3).
9. **Footer** — secondary link columns (Product, Company, Support), social links as Material icons, copyright, mini wordmark.

**0.3 Copy Voice**
Write all user-facing copy in **English**, in an original Fairycore voice (dreamy, whimsical, enchanted-garden product narrative — e.g., a fairy-garden subscription kit). **No lorem ipsum.** Every interactive control gets a real, descriptive label.

---

## 1. STRICT RULES & ARCHITECTURE

**1.1 CSS-First Architecture & Zero Inline CSS**
* **No Inline CSS:** The `style="..."` attribute, inline `<style>` blocks, and presentation attributes are **forbidden**.
* **Class/ID Selectors Only:** All design properties, layout rules, and states must be targeted via class or ID selectors in `style.css`.
* **Minimal HTML Modifications:** HTML must remain clean, semantic, and style-agnostic — re-theming the site requires touching only the CSS file, never the markup.

**1.2 CSS Variables & Theme Tokens**
Store **all** visual tokens in `:root` (light) and `.dark` (dark) using this canonical contract. Where the reference spec's names differ, define both and consume the canonical names in components (mapping: `--color-bg` ≡ `--bg-primary`, `--color-surface` ≡ `--bg-secondary`, `--color-text` ≡ `--text-primary`, `--color-text-muted` ≡ `--text-secondary`, `--color-border` ≡ `--border-default`, `--color-primary` ≡ `--primary`, `--color-accent` ≡ `--secondary`/`--accent`):

```css
/* FAIRYCORE — canonical design token contract (light) */
/* Reference spec: references/00-flagship-implementation-specs/fairycore.md */
:root {
  /* Mandatory canonical colors */
  --primary: #c9679a;          /* luminous rose */
  --secondary: #8fb98a;        /* soft moss */
  --bg-primary: #fdf3f8;       /* pastel blush page bg — never #ffffff */
  --bg-secondary: #fffdfb;     /* near-white warm surface */
  --text-primary: #4a2b45;     /* deep plum */
  --text-secondary: #7a5573;   /* muted mauve */
  --text-success: #2f6134;     /* deep moss */
  --text-error: #b23a48;      /* deep rose-red */
  --border-default: #e7bfd9;
  --border-error: #e3a2ae;
  --border-success: #a8c9a0;
  --on-primary: #fff7fb;       /* text paired onto --primary fills */

  /* Fairycore extended tokens */
  --color-bg-gradient-a: #f6e3f5;
  --color-bg-gradient-b: #e3f0e6;
  --color-surface-strong: #fbeaf3;
  --color-glow: #fff3c4;
  --accent: #8fb98a;

  /* Radius / shadow */
  --radius-sm: 10px; --radius-md: 18px; --radius-lg: 28px; --radius-pill: 999px;
  --shadow-sm: 0 2px 8px rgba(201,103,154,0.16);
  --shadow-md: 0 8px 24px rgba(201,103,154,0.20);
  --shadow-lg: 0 16px 40px rgba(201,103,154,0.24);
  --shadow-glow: 0 0 24px rgba(255,243,196,0.55);

  /* Spacing / transitions / elevation */
  --spacing-gap: 16px;
  --transition-fast: 150ms; --transition-normal: 250ms;
  --ease-standard: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
  --ease-entrance: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0, 1);
  --z-dropdown: 1000; --z-modal: 1100; --z-toast: 1200;

  /* Typography — retain the full --text-xs…--text-5xl and --space-1…--space-24 scales from the reference spec */
  --font-base: 'Quicksand', 'Nunito', system-ui, sans-serif;
  --font-display: 'Cormorant Garamond', 'Parisienne', Georgia, serif;

  /* Signature effects */
  --bg-image: radial-gradient(60% 50% at 15% 0%, var(--color-bg-gradient-b) 0%, transparent 60%),
              radial-gradient(70% 60% at 100% 20%, var(--color-bg-gradient-a) 0%, transparent 65%),
              var(--bg-primary);
  --sparkle-field: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(255,255,255,0.9) 0 1px, transparent 1.5px) 0 0/26px 26px,
                   radial-gradient(circle, rgba(255,243,196,0.8) 0 1px, transparent 1.5px) 13px 13px/26px 26px;
}
```

* **Contrast Pairing:** Every light background token must pair with a dark text token and every dark background token with a light text token — enforced **per theme**. Primary fills must use `--on-primary` for their text.
* **Light Mode Background:** Never pure white; the spec's `#fffdfb` is the near-white. Use `#fefefe` only if an extra near-white is genuinely needed.
* **Dark Tokens (mandatory — the source spec declares no modes; you must author them and validate contrast in BOTH light and dark before publishing):**

```css
.dark {
  --bg-primary: #211726;        /* deep enchanted plum */
  --bg-secondary: #2b1f31;      /* plum surface */
  --color-surface-strong: #3a2a44;
  --text-primary: #f6e9f3;      /* moonlit lace */
  --text-secondary: #c9aec6;
  --primary: #e79bc6;           /* luminous rose, lightened for dark bg */
  --on-primary: #331229;        /* dark text on the light rose fill */
  --secondary: #a4c9a0; --accent: #a4c9a0;
  --border-default: #4d3756;
  --border-error: #8a4a56; --border-success: #4a6b48;
  --text-success: #a8d8a4; --text-error: #f0a3ae;
  --color-bg-gradient-a: #3a2440; --color-bg-gradient-b: #22352a;
  --shadow-sm: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);
  --shadow-md: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.45);
  --shadow-lg: 0 16px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.55);
  --shadow-glow: 0 0 24px rgba(255,243,196,0.30);
  --sparkle-field: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(255,255,255,0.35) 0 1px, transparent 1.5px) 0 0/26px 26px,
                   radial-gradient(circle, rgba(255,243,196,0.45) 0 1px, transparent 1.5px) 13px 13px/26px 26px;
}
```

**1.3 Mandatory Dark Mode Support**
* **Implementation:** Provide dark tokens under **both** `@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)` (applied to `:root:not(.light)`) **and** a `.dark` class on `<html>`; the explicit class always overrides the media query. Declare `color-scheme` per theme so native controls and scrollbars match.
* **Theme Switching:** Background and text variables must flip with **zero HTML restructuring** and no duplicated stylesheets.
* **Persistence:** Store the user's choice in `localStorage`; on first visit fall back to `prefers-color-scheme`. Apply the stored choice in the deferred `script.js` as early as possible (the media-query base prevents a wrong-theme flash for system-preference users without requiring any inline script).
* **Toggle Control:** A visible toggle in the nav with a Material icon (`dark_mode` / `light_mode`), correct `aria-pressed` and `aria-label` ("Switch to dark mode" / "Switch to light mode"), and visible focus state.

**1.4 Flexbox Layout & Mobile-First Alignment**
* Build all layout structures with Flexbox (`display: flex` / Tailwind flex utilities).
* **Default Alignment Rule:** Every flex container defaults to `align-items: center` (`items-center`) unless an exception is explicitly justified in a CSS comment.
* **Mobile-Friendly First:** Rows convert to columns on small viewports (~<640px); fluid type via `clamp()` is encouraged; **horizontal scrolling is prohibited** in any viewport.

**1.5 Framework Default & Tailwind CSS Integration**
* Use **Tailwind CSS** (Play CDN or compiled) with custom component classes defined via `@layer` / `@apply` in `style.css`.
* All utilities and components must map back to the CSS variables above or to generic reusable class names (`.nav`, `.btn`, `.card`, `.input`, `.badge`, `.input-group`). **Never hardcode hex values in component rules** — reference `var(--…)`.

**1.6 Typography & Icons (Google Fonts Mandatory)**
* **Text:** Include Google Font `<link>` tags for **Quicksand** (400–700, bound to `--font-base`) and **Cormorant Garamond** (500–700, italic included, bound to `--font-display`); **Parisienne** may be loaded for one decorative flourish (e.g., a single accented word in the hero) only.
* **Icons:** Use **Google Material Symbols** (Rounded style — it suits the soft aesthetic) via `<span class="material-symbols-rounded">icon_name</span>`. **Inline SVGs and local icon files are forbidden.** Decorative icons get `aria-hidden="true"`; meaningful icons get accessible labels.

---

## 2. COMPONENT DESIGN SPECIFICATIONS

**2.1 Button Component**
Style all states via CSS classes; baseline: `font: 600 var(--text-base)/1 var(--font-base)`, `padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-6)`, `border-radius: var(--radius-pill)`, surface background, `1px solid var(--border-default)`, `box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm)`, `min-height: 44px` (44×44px touch target).
* **Default:** `display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.5rem; cursor: pointer;`
* **Hover:** `transform: translateY(-1px)` and `box-shadow: var(--shadow-md), var(--shadow-glow)`.
* **Focus:** Distinct `:focus-visible` ring — `outline: 2px solid var(--primary); outline-offset: 2px`.
* **Active/Pressed:** `transform: scale(0.97)` click feedback.
* **Loading:** `aria-busy="true"`; disables interaction and prevents double-clicks; renders a CSS spinner ring or animated Material icon **without changing button dimensions**.
* **Disabled:** `opacity: 0.5`, greyscale filter, `cursor: not-allowed`, no hover/active effects.
* **Success/Error:** Temporary `.btn--success` / `.btn--error` feedback styles driven by `--text-success` / `--text-error`, announced via an `aria-live` region.
* **Variants:** `.btn--primary` (background `var(--primary)`, color `var(--on-primary)`), `.btn--ghost`, and `.btn--danger` — the danger variant must be visually distinct in **both** themes.

**2.2 Card Component**
Baseline: `background: var(--bg-secondary); background-image: var(--sparkle-field); border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); box-shadow: var(--shadow-md), var(--shadow-glow); padding: var(--space-6);` — applied to feature, testimonial, and pricing cards.
* **Default:** Flexible flexbox layout, `align-items: center` where appropriate.
* **Hover:** `transform: translateY(-2px)` with elevation shift to `--shadow-lg` + glow.
* **Focus-within:** Card border highlights (`--primary`) when a child link/button receives focus.
* **Loading (Skeleton):** Shimmer keyframe animation defined in CSS to prevent layout jumps.
* **Empty State:** Structured fallback layout with a Material icon and clear guidance text.

**2.3 Form & Input Requirements**
Structure each field as a flex `.input-group` wrapping a `<label>`, the input, and a dedicated error-feedback container. Baseline input: `background: var(--color-surface-strong); border: 1px solid var(--border-default); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4); color: var(--text-primary);` with placeholder color `var(--text-secondary)`.
* **States:** Empty, Focused (`border-color: var(--primary)` + `box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(201,103,154,0.22), var(--shadow-glow)`), Filled, Valid (`--border-success` + check icon), Invalid (`--border-error`, error text in `--text-error`, error icon, message rendered in an `aria-live="polite"` container), Disabled, Read-only.
* The **Final CTA newsletter form** must implement the full flow: submit → loading (spinner, no double-submit) → success or error feedback, all visually and accessibly announced.

**2.4 Modal / Popup & Accordion Requirements**
* **FAQ Accordion:** Disclosure buttons with `aria-expanded` / `aria-controls`, chevron rotation, smooth CSS height transition (`grid-template-rows: 0fr → 1fr` or equivalent), keyboard operable (Enter/Space), and reduced-motion safe.
* **Modal (if any, e.g., plan details):** Animated Opening, Open, Loading, Success/Error, and Closing states via CSS transitions; centered flex container (`align-items: center`) with backdrop overlay at `--z-modal`; Material `close` icon button; keyboard focus trapping; close via `Esc` and overlay click; `role="dialog"` + `aria-modal="true"`.

---

## 3. CORE UX & MICRO-INTERACTION RULES

* **Responsive by Default:** Fluid sizing and breakpoints with zero horizontal overflow at every viewport width.
* **Smooth Animations:** `transition: var(--transition-normal) var(--ease-standard)` on all state changes; globally respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` by disabling transforms, shimmer, and decorative motion (extend the reference spec's existing reduce block).
* **Accessibility (a11y):** Body-text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 in **both light and dark modes** — validate before publishing. Never rely on color alone to communicate state (pair color with icons and text). Use semantic HTML5 landmarks (`header`, `nav`, `main`, `section[aria-labelledby]`, `footer`), a skip-to-content link, correct ARIA roles/labels on custom widgets, logical DOM/focus order, full keyboard operability (no mouse-only interactions), visible focus rings everywhere, and `aria-live` regions for dynamic feedback (form errors, toasts, loading states).
* **Mandatory Visual Feedback:** Every click, hover, and submission triggers a visible state change.
* **Destructive Actions:** `.btn--danger` / delete actions must be visually distinct in both themes.
* **Fairycore Motion:** Optional gentle decorative animations (drifting sparkle/petal keyframes) are allowed — `aria-hidden`, purely decorative, paused under reduced motion, and never placed where they impair readability.

---

## 4. DELIVERABLE & OUTPUT FORMAT

* **File Structure:** Separate `index.html`, `style.css`, and `script.js`. No inline `<style>` blocks and no inline `<script>` blocks beyond a **single** `<script src="script.js" defer></script>` entry point.
* **Naming Convention:** Enforce **BEM** consistently across the entire deliverable (e.g., `.btn--primary`, `.card__title`, `.input-group__error`) — matching the reference spec's `.btn--primary` pattern. Never mix conventions.
* **No Unrequested Placeholders:** All copy, labels, and alt/ARIA text must be real, on-theme English content. Lorem ipsum is prohibited; placeholders are allowed only where content was genuinely left unspecified by the user.
* **First-Attempt Completeness & Pre-Publication Validation:** Deliver complete, runnable code in one pass — then verify: (a) light **and** dark mode both render correctly with the toggle persisting via `localStorage`; (b) contrast passes in both modes (the source spec declares no modes — this validation is mandatory before publishing); (c) full keyboard pass with visible focus; (d) no console errors; (e) all nine sections from Rule 0.2 present and anchored; (f) zero inline styles and zero horizontal scroll.
